+Dispositions:
+- `KEEP`: Well-architected, security-essential control functioning with complete backend parity.
+- `SIMPLIFY`: Functional control that requires clearer labels, intuitive units, preset buttons, or streamlined UX.
+- `MERGE`: Separate controls that should be unified into a single coherent interface card or modal.
+- `MOVE_TO_ADVANCED`: High-risk or niche configuration that should be tucked inside collapsible progressive disclosure (`<AdvancedSection>`) to reduce primary visual clutter.
+- `CUT`: Redundant input, dead control, or static placeholder that provides no operational utility.
